CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ member of a local thrown: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ local object thrown: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The THROW read its operand when lowered, after the destructors of the
try block had run, so it copied a destroyed object.  goto conversion now
copies the operand into a temporary before the destructors.
